1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:03,762
Pole inspection photos leave a reviewer with three questions.

2
00:00:04,553 --> 00:00:06,212
Is there a visible concern?

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,607
Has the asset changed?

4
00:00:09,395 --> 00:00:12,423
Is the image clear enough to support either conclusion?

5
00:00:13,211 --> 00:00:17,015
Camera movement and poor contrast can make those decisions harder.

6
00:00:17,803 --> 00:00:21,947
SpanWitness keeps the photos, supported image measurements and next

7
00:00:21,947 --> 00:00:24,554
inspection step together for each asset.

8
00:00:25,342 --> 00:00:28,449
OpenCV 5 is the image-processing engine.

9
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:33,355
It checks sharpness, detects edges with Canny and finds long line

10
00:00:33,355 --> 00:00:35,383
candidates with a Hough transform.

11
00:00:36,171 --> 00:00:40,605
Inside the operator-marked pole and reference regions, Huber line fitting

12
00:00:40,605 --> 00:00:42,554
estimates their orientations.

13
00:00:43,342 --> 00:00:45,870
The app then compares those image angles.

14
00:00:46,658 --> 00:00:49,936
The same pipeline runs on Amazon Web Services.

15
00:00:50,737 --> 00:00:53,528
API Gateway sends requests to Lambda.

16
00:00:54,316 --> 00:01:00,289
Private S3 stores images, and DynamoDB stores observations, comparisons and

17
00:01:00,289 --> 00:01:01,528
review requests.

18
00:01:02,316 --> 00:01:05,699
Now let's follow one inspection in the working application.

19
00:01:06,487 --> 00:01:09,789
This is a real, openly licensed photo of a pole beside

20
00:01:09,789 --> 00:01:10,488
a house.

21
00:01:11,289 --> 00:01:14,686
The gold and blue marks select the pole and building reference.

22
00:01:15,474 --> 00:01:20,633
After analysis, the measured difference is 19.3 degrees in this photograph.

23
00:01:21,421 --> 00:01:23,923
It is not a measurement of physical pole lean.

24
00:01:24,711 --> 00:01:27,791
The app proposes a structural alignment inspection.

25
00:01:28,579 --> 00:01:32,658
A reviewer can inspect the original and annotated images, add a

26
00:01:32,658 --> 00:01:35,133
note and confirm a provisional request.

27
00:01:35,921 --> 00:01:38,712
The saved record keeps the evidence attached.

28
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,173
No external crew notification is sent.

29
00:01:42,961 --> 00:01:46,331
A second real photograph demonstrates the other outcome.

30
00:01:47,118 --> 00:01:50,212
Here, the marked pole edge lacks enough support.

31
00:01:51,013 --> 00:01:54,896
The app returns no angle and requests a clearer observation.

32
00:01:55,697 --> 00:01:59,067
These are different assets, not a before-and-after pair.

33
00:01:59,868 --> 00:02:04,316
For dated observations of the same asset, history compares a baseline

34
00:02:04,316 --> 00:02:05,765
with a later inspection.

35
00:02:06,566 --> 00:02:11,475
OpenCV uses ORB features and RANSAC to check the shared background.

36
00:02:12,276 --> 00:02:16,567
Reference and perspective checks can reject unsuitable comparisons.

37
00:02:17,355 --> 00:02:20,962
Repeatable capture and a fixed reference are still required.

38
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:26,488
The history example shown here uses synthetic scenes and illustrative dates.

39
00:02:27,276 --> 00:02:32,054
The deployment view shows the actual hosted address and OpenCV runtime.

40
00:02:32,855 --> 00:02:38,355
In AWS, we read back the same real-photo observation from DynamoDB

41
00:02:38,355 --> 00:02:41,304
and verify the stored image hash in S3.

42
00:02:42,105 --> 00:02:47,120
62 software tests and 108 controlled history checks passed.

43
00:02:47,921 --> 00:02:52,408
The two real photos are selected demonstrations, not a field accuracy

44
00:02:52,408 --> 00:02:53,278
benchmark.

45
00:02:54,066 --> 00:02:58,355
This prototype does not diagnose cracks, predict a pole falling or

46
00:02:58,355 --> 00:03:00,291
calculate fire probability.

47
00:03:01,079 --> 00:03:04,171
Its purpose is to help an inspector decide what to review

48
00:03:04,171 --> 00:03:07,225
next, with the evidence and its limits attached.

49
00:03:08,013 --> 00:03:11,067
I am Kumar Abhinav, and this is SpanWitness.
